te [[Cookbook:Rice and Lentils (Mejadra)|rice]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] unsalted [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Tsp|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ tsp freshly-ground [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 ½ cups low-sodium [[Cookbook:Chicken Broth|chicken broth]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Red Wine|red wine]], preferably Chianti\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n* 7 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], smashed\n* 10 sprigs fresh [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* 5–6 sprigs fresh [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n* 1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Melt butter in a large [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] over medium high heat. Add rice and onion and cook until rice is golden.\n#Meanwhile, combine remaining ingredients. Once rice has toasted, remove from pot and add mixture. Bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] and add rice. Cook, stirring occasionally, 30 minutes or until rice is desired tenderness.\n#Serve warm with a steak, a glass of red wine, and maybe a vegetable sauté.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rosemary]]\n[[Category:Recipes using thyme]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Italian Rice Pilaf","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups uncooked white rice","sourceText":"2 cups uncooked white rice","amountText":"2 cups uncooked white rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","sourceText":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","amountText":"2 tbsp unsalted butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ 